  "2026-11-17T09:04:10.935Z",codex-sol,"Round AP verification: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS; git diff --check => PASS. Focused suite: ℹ tests 185, ℹ pass 185, ℹ fail 0, ℹ cancelled 0, ℹ skipped 0, ℹ todo 0. Every real workflow still passes; all prior fixtures retained. Guard md5 e882f7b9396d4a810ccf85250dc05a04. No configured lint, duplicates script."
  "2026-11-17T10:20:42.270Z",codex-sol,"Round AR: reproduced assignment-valued short-flag, renamed-archive, quoted-expression and uppercase Boolean bypasses against the unchanged shared guard. Preserve dual line scans and all fixtures; replace global operand inference with a registry-spec allowlist, normalize option names before marker tests and compare env values exactly. Run the round AN gates and regenerate changelog after all tracker writes. Leave this item open."
  "2026-11-17T10:25:31.328Z",codex-sol,"Round AR implementation and validation: PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864Xamy. Global install operands now require the plain registry name-spec allowlist and exclude npm identities; archive, path, URL, git, alias, computed and quote-fragment operands reject. Option names are unquoted and split before assignment-valued marker tests. Env keys ignore case but safe global/location values compare exactly, including run assignments. Both physical and joined scans and bootstrap exemptions remain. Preserved all prior fixtures; focused guard: 202/202; round AN contract gate: 223/223; typecheck passed. All real workflows pass the guard. Guard md5: 1b36b35bf3ce5df79ae313b939f17971. Final tracker writes precede tag refresh and changelog regeneration/check; keep the item in_progress and release the claim. No review thread mutations or workflow dispatches."
  "2026-11-17T10:52:49.496Z",codex-sol,"Round AS: verified current code before editing. The line union omits PowerShell backticks and the workflow extractor omits container and service env scopes. Add LF/CRLF and effective-env regressions, preserve all existing fixtures, and keep all five guard copies identical."
  "2026-11-17T10:59:30.973Z",codex-sol,"Round AS: addressed the shared findings PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64YXiD and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64YXiL from pm-ops#289. Verified both bypasses against the previous guard; new fixtures failed before fixes and pass after them. Scan the union of normalized physical lines, joined backslashes and joined PowerShell backticks, with LF/CRLF fixtures. Compose container defaults with workflow/job/step scopes; conservatively check service env scopes independently so one safe service cannot mask another unsafe service. Unsupported container env fails closed. Retained all approved/rejected fixtures and real workflow checks. No equivalent overlapping-install test exists here. Main gates passed 225/225; additional coverage-gate references 31/31; build and typecheck passed. All five guard copies have md5 a515dca0fd6175db9bcb1dc5c780989c. No findings refused. Changelog generation/check follows final tracker writes; CI is not yet verified."
  "2026-11-17T11:09:12.611Z",codex-sol,"Changelog preservation check found four published main bullets absent from the existing branch. Separate merge 76b7393 restores main before the AS code commit, without folding new guard edits or their tracker records into that merge. Restored the updated lock with npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund. The expanded referencing-file run includes the main CI/caller changes and every test mentioning the merged package metadata; it is currently exercising synchronization boundary matrices. Final results and tracker release precede another full changelog generation/check."
  "2026-11-17T11:59:27.011Z",codex-sol,"Scope correction: the 17-file expanded run included package metadata imported unchanged from main, although package.json and package-lock.json are absent from the AS diff against updated main. That optional stress run passed every initial boundary matrix and all 500 seeded sequences with 500 exact and 50 older replay checks, but was intentionally stopped during the separate 512-sequence concurrency model; no aggregate success is claimed. The original guard gates had passed. Re-running the required guard/workflow files plus their direct references and the imported CI/caller contracts on the final source before commit. The optional interrupted command is retained as evidence, not as a passing AS gate."
